cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the CatCrypt paper below."
title: "Verified native evaluation for Lean"
abstract: >-
  A decision procedure written in a fragment of Lean is compiled to x86-64
  bytes by a compiler proved correct for every program of the fragment, and a
  closed decidable proposition follows from one run of a fixed x86 machine
  model on those bytes. The tactics verified_decide, verified_decide_hw and
  verified_decide_lit replace native_decide where the decision procedure's
  compiled code is to be left out of the trusted base.
type: software
authors:
